<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Required for @capacitor/push-notifications.

  WHY "production" AND NOT "development"

  aps-environment names which APNs host the device token minted for this build
  belongs to. A token is not portable between the two: a token issued under
  "development" is rejected by api.push.apple.com, and vice versa, with a
  400 BadDeviceToken that says nothing about why.

  Every build of this app that is SIGNED is a Release build produced by the
  testflight job in .github/workflows/ios-build.yml, bound for TestFlight or
  the App Store. Both of those are the production host. So "production" is not
  a release-time switch anyone has to remember to flip — it is simply the only
  value that is ever correct here.

  The matching half is server-side: _shared/apns.js picks its host from
  APNS_PRODUCTION, so that must be set to true in Netlify or the backend will
  keep posting production tokens to the sandbox host. Both halves or neither.

  WHY THE DEBUG CONFIGURATION DOES NOT REFERENCE THIS FILE

  CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS is set on the Release build configuration only. Debug
  exists here solely to answer "does it compile?" on a simulator, unsigned
  (see the compile job in the same workflow), and the simulator cannot register
  with APNs at all — so an entitlement there would buy nothing while giving the
  one currently-green job a provisioning profile it does not have and does not
  need.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>production</string>
</dict>
</plist>
